n"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008517"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008531"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008542"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008559"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008572"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008594"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008609"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008621"} "Canadian Singles, 200 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016295"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/2577"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2180"} "National Olympic Nautical Stadium d'Île-de-France, Vaires-sur-Marne, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2008638"} "26 from 13 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Women were competing in Canadian events for only the second time at the Olympics, after Tokyo 2020. The defending champions in this event were the Chinese duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/141665"} "Xu Shixiao"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141663"} "Sun Mengya"] ". They were favored, having won the World Championships in 2019, 2022, and 2023, although they were only world ranked #2 coming into Paris. The #1 spot was held by the Hungarian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/151249"} "Bianka Nagy"] " and Giada Bragato, but Bragato would not compete in Paris, as Nagy was accompanied by " [:a {:href "/athletes/151247"} "Ágnes Kiss"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Xu and Sun were dominant, setting Olympic best times in heat one of round one (1:54.45), the first semi-final, with 1:53.73, and in winning the final in 1:52.81. The Canadian double of " [:a {:href "/athletes/151189"} "Sloan Mackenzie"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141380"} "Katie Vincent"] " bettered China’s round one best time with 1:54.16 in heat two, and also won the second semi-final, but they were no match in the final for the Chinese pair, as Xu and Sun defended their gold medal by almost 1½ seconds over the Ukrainian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/2102690"} "Liudmyla Luzan"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/147015"} "Anastasiya Rybachok"] ", with Mackenzie and Vincent taking bronze."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The medal podium was almost exactly the same as it had been at Tokyo 2020, with Xu and Sun on top. Luzan and Rybachok won their second consecutive silver in the event, as Rybachok had raced in 2020 under her maiden name of Anastasiya Chetverikova, while for Vincent it was a second consecutive bronze medal in the event, having finished third at Tokyo 2020 with " [:a {:href "/athletes/141381"} "Laurence Vincent-Lapointe"] " (no relation). The day after this event ended, Vincent would win gold in the C1-200."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141665"} "Xu Shixiao"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/141663"} "Sun Mengya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "C